  "rationale": "Blocking mailClient:execution, tokenCache:credentialAccess and fileServer:lateralMovement makes the target unreachable. Blocking mailClient stops vpnSession and rdpLogin. That in turn stops monitoringHost, hypervisor, secretsManager and serviceAccount, so dbReplica and shareMount are cut off. Blocking tokenCache stops ssoLogin, apiToken and the tokenCache branch of printServer, which cuts off mailArchive and localAdmin. Blocking fileServer removes codeRepo's last parent, since browserStore and vpnSession both reach codeRepo only through fileServer. Fewer than 3 is impossible because there are three attack paths that share no blockable step. Path one is internet -> browserStore -> fileServer -> codeRepo. Path two is containerHost -> tokenCache -> printServer -> mailArchive. Path three is sshKey + mailClient -> vpnSession -> monitoringHost -> dbReplica. Each path needs its own block."
 },
